# REQUIRES: python-api, hdf5, cuda
# The estimate of the shift (D210) under a barostat, on a GPU (#224): after the cell
# has changed, what the correction for the dispersion adds equals its
# closed forms at the present volume in every place that takes the
# estimate: the columns of `observe`, the energy under the shift,
# `gradient()` and its energy (D230) from Python; the potential, the
# observables file, and dH/dlambda of `mdir run`. Double and mixed.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/pair_tail_system.py %t 60 60 32 3.7 0.5
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/shift_volume.py %t GPU mdir %t | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: GPU Double Python: at V/V0 = 0.9{{[0-9]+}} the correction adds its closed forms at the present volume to the columns of observe, to the energy under the shift, and to gradient() and its energy
# CHECK: GPU Double mdir run: at V/V0 = 0.9{{[0-9]+}} the correction adds its closed forms at the present volume to the potential under the shift, to the observables file, and to dH/dlambda
# CHECK: GPU Mixed Python: at V/V0
# CHECK: GPU Mixed mdir run: at V/V0
# CHECK: shift volume passed
